.Dd October 14, 2026
.Dt XFT 7
.Os xft
.Sh NAME
.Nm xft
.Nd freestanding C23 systems library
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In xft.h
.Ft void
.Fn xft_main "const t_any *__restrict__ const sp"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a freestanding C23 library for Linux and 64-bit Windows on x86_64 and
aarch64.
It replaces the parts of libc a program normally relies on and links with
.Fl nostdlib .
A hosted flavor, selected with
.Fl Duse-libc ,
exposes the same API on a normal toolchain.
.Pp
Programs include
.In xft.h ,
which pulls in every public header, and define
.Fn xft_main
instead of
.Fn main .
.Fn xft_main
receives the initial stack pointer, from which the runtime helpers recover
the arguments, environment and auxiliary vector, and must end with
.Fn xft_exit ;
see
.Xr xft_rt 3 .
.Ss Conventions
.Bl -bullet
.It
Every public symbol is prefixed
.Ql xft_ .
.It
Fallible functions return
.Vt t_result ,
which is
.Dv OK
(1) or
.Dv KO
(0).
There is no
.Va errno .
.It
Containers and allocating functions take the allocator explicitly as a
.Vt t_allocator
argument and, where the element type is not fixed, the element size in bytes.
See
.Xr xft_alloc 3 .
.It
Integer and floating-point typedefs are fixed-width and encode alignment in
the name: the plain type has alignment 1 and is safe for unaligned access,
the
.Ql a
suffix carries natural alignment.
All primitive typedefs are
.Ql may_alias .
.El
.Ss Primitive types
Declared in
.In primitives.h :
.Bl -column "t_u128, t_u128a" "unsigned 128-bit (__uint128_t)"
.It Vt t_u8 , t_i8 Ta 8-bit integers
.It Vt t_u16 , t_u16a Ta 16-bit unsigned
.It Vt t_i16 , t_i16a Ta 16-bit signed
.It Vt t_u32 , t_u32a Ta 32-bit unsigned
.It Vt t_i32 , t_i32a Ta 32-bit signed
.It Vt t_u64 , t_u64a Ta 64-bit unsigned
.It Vt t_i64 , t_i64a Ta 64-bit signed
.It Vt t_u128 , t_u128a Ta unsigned 128-bit (__uint128_t)
.It Vt t_i128 , t_i128a Ta signed 128-bit (__int128_t)
.It Vt t_f32 , t_f32a Ta float
.It Vt t_f64 , t_f64a Ta double
.It Vt t_f80 , t_f80a Ta long double
.It Vt t_uptr Ta pointer-sized unsigned integer
.It Vt t_any , t_cany Ta void pointer, const void pointer
.It Vt t_size Ta alias of t_u64
.It Vt t_ssize Ta alias of t_i64
.El
.Pp
Compound types:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
typedef struct s_buffer {
	t_size	size;
	t_u8	*mem;	/* counted_by(size) under clang */
} t_buffer;

typedef enum e_result { OK = 1, KO = 0 } t_result;

typedef struct s_span {
	t_size	typesize;
	t_size	n;
} t_span;
.Ed
.Pp
.In macros.h
defines ANSI escape strings:
.Dv ANSI_RESET ,
the foreground colors
.Dv ANSI_BLACK
through
.Dv ANSI_WHITE ,
their bold
.Dv ANSI_B*
variants, and the background colors
.Dv ANSI_BG_RED
through
.Dv ANSI_BG_WHITE .
.Ss Platform checks
.In primitives.h
rejects the build with
.Ic #error
when compiling freestanding on an architecture other than x86_64 or
aarch64 without
.Dv XFT_REQUIRE_LIBC ,
on 32-bit Windows, and on any operating system other than Linux or Win64.
.Dv XFT_REQUIRE_LIBC
is defined by the build when
.Fl Duse-libc
is set.
.Ss Subsystems
.Bl -tag -width "xft_swissmap(3)"
.It Xr xft_alloc 3
allocator interface, arena, general purpose, page and reporting allocators
.It Xr xft_atomics 3
mutexes and atomic types
.It Xr xft_bmi 3
bit manipulation and SIMD mask primitives
.It Xr xft_cstr 3
NUL-terminated string functions
.It Xr xft_ctype 3
character classification
.It Xr xft_fmt 3
formatted output
.It Xr xft_fuzzer 3
fuzzing harness
.It Xr xft_hash 3
hash functions
.It Xr xft_hint 3
runtime invariants and optimizer hints
.It Xr xft_indexmap 3
insertion-ordered hash map
.It Xr xft_io 3
file descriptors and buffered input/output
.It Xr xft_math 3
math functions
.It Xr xft_mem 3
memory copy, move, set and compare
.It Xr xft_rng 3
pseudo-random number generation
.It Xr xft_rt 3
program entry point and runtime
.It Xr xft_signals 3
signal handling
.It Xr xft_soa 3
structure-of-arrays container
.It Xr xft_sort 3
sorting
.It Xr xft_str 3
growable strings
.It Xr xft_swissmap 3
SIMD open-addressing hash map
.It Xr xft_syscalls 3
system call wrappers
.It Xr xft_timing 3
clocks and cycle counters
.It Xr xft_vec 3
growable arrays
.It Xr xft_xid 3
Unicode XID_Start and XID_Continue lookup and UTF-8 decoding
.El
.Sh BUILD OPTIONS
.Nm
builds with Zig 0.17.0 or later, whose bundled Clang
compiles the C sources:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
zig build -Doptimize=fast
.Ed
.Pp
The build installs into
.Pa zig-out/ :
.Pa lib/libxft.a
.Pq Pa lib/xft.lib No on Windows
and the headers under
.Pa include/xft/ .
On Linux it also installs
.Pa lib/libxft-perf.a
and
.Pa lib/libxft-tailor.a ,
see
.Sx PERF AND TAILOR .
Zig consumers link the
.Ql xft
artifact of the dependency, which carries the headers, the Windows import
libraries, and on Linux
.Nm perf
and
.Nm tailor .
.Bl -tag -width "-Dfast-math"
.It Fl Doptimize
.Ql debug ,
.Ql safe ,
.Ql fast
or
.Ql small .
.Ql fast
and
.Ql safe
also add
.Fl O3 .
Default
.Ql debug .
.It Fl Dtarget
The target triple, such as
.Ql x86_64-linux
or
.Ql x86_64-windows-gnu .
Default the host.
.It Fl Dcpu
The CPU model and features, such as
.Ql native ,
.Ql baseline
or
.Ql x86_64_v3 .
Every ISA path in
.Nm
follows it.
Default
.Ql native .
.It Fl Duse-libc
Build against a libc instead of freestanding.
Default off.
.It Fl Dsanitize
UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer and stack checks; Zig ships no AddressSanitizer
runtime.
Requires
.Fl Duse-libc
and disables LTO.
Default off.
.It Fl Dlto
Full link-time optimization.
Default off.
.It Fl Dfast-math
Compile with
.Fl ffast-math .
Default off.
.It Fl Dllc
Last level cache size in bytes, defining
.Dv XFT_LLC_SIZE ,
above which
.Fn xft_memcpy
and
.Fn xft_memset
switch to non-temporal stores.
Default 16777216.
.It Fl Dtests
Build the unit tests, always sanitized, and the
.Cm test
step that runs them.
.It Fl Dfuzz
Build the fuzz targets and the
.Cm fuzz
step that runs them.
Requires
.Fl Dsanitize
and
.Fl Duse-libc .
.It Fl Dbenches
Build the benchmarks and the
.Cm run-bench
step that runs them.
Requires
.Fl Doptimize=fast ,
no
.Fl Dsanitize ,
and Linux.
.It Fl Dbootstrap
Build the library without the xid module, build
.Nm gentable ,
and regenerate its table from
.Pa DerivedCoreProperties.txt
in the source root.
Cannot be combined with
.Fl Dtests .
See
.Xr xft_xid 3 .
.El
.Pp
Warnings are always errors.
.Sh PERF AND TAILOR
On Linux,
.Nm
builds two more libraries on top of
.Xr perf_event_open 2 ,
compiled with the same flavor as the library itself:
.Bl -tag -width "tailor"
.It Nm perf
.In xft/perf.h :
hardware and software performance counter groups, sampling, and CPU
pinning.
.It Nm tailor
.In xft/tailor.h :
the benchmark harness used by
.Pa bench/ ,
built on
.Nm perf .
.El
.Pp
Both link
.Nm
and are linked by it in the Zig build.
Linking the archives by hand, they go before
.Nm :
.Fl lxft-tailor Fl lxft-perf Fl lxft .
They are not built for Windows.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
#include <xft.h>

void	xft_main(const t_any *__restrict__ const sp)
{
	(void)sp;
	xft_exit(0);
}
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr xft_alloc 3 ,
.Xr xft_io 3 ,
.Xr xft_rt 3 ,
.Xr xft_xid 3
